1
00:00:14,914 --> 00:00:16,383
KANBARA DOCTOR AGENCY

2
00:00:16,449 --> 00:00:19,586
ALBERTO SAVAROTTI

3
00:00:26,326 --> 00:00:27,460
I'm going.

4
00:00:28,028 --> 00:00:29,829
What's with your costume?

5
00:00:29,896 --> 00:00:32,866
Tomorrow will be the best day ever.

6
00:00:33,666 --> 00:00:34,634
Best day?

7
00:00:34,701 --> 00:00:36,536
Look.

8
00:00:37,470 --> 00:00:38,438
Who's this?

9
00:00:38,505 --> 00:00:39,539
You don't know?

10
00:00:39,606 --> 00:00:43,109
The greatest opera singer,
Alberto Savarotti.

11
00:00:43,743 --> 00:00:44,744
No clue.

12
00:00:44,811 --> 00:00:46,212
Forget it.

13
00:00:46,279 --> 00:00:48,548
His concert is tomorrow.

14
00:00:49,716 --> 00:00:51,484
Dressed already?

15
00:00:51,551 --> 00:00:53,253
It can be in 3 days.

16
00:00:53,319 --> 00:00:54,821
A fan would get ready.

17
00:00:54,888 --> 00:00:56,256
Bye.

18
00:00:56,322 --> 00:00:59,259
- Wait. Talk to me a bit more.
- Bye.

19
00:00:59,325 --> 00:01:00,994
Play along with me.

20
00:01:01,061 --> 00:01:06,399
Active export of Japan's
quality medical services is needed.

21
00:01:06,466 --> 00:01:09,903
How should the future
of Japan's healthcare be?

22
00:01:10,570 --> 00:01:14,174
I'd like to think
about this with the viewers.

23
00:01:14,240 --> 00:01:16,376
Our guest is Mr. Tendo,

24
00:01:16,443 --> 00:01:21,714
president of the National Advanced
Medical Care Center.

25
00:01:21,781 --> 00:01:23,283
I'm Tendo.

26
00:01:25,518 --> 00:01:28,421
Our Medical Care Center

27
00:01:28,488 --> 00:01:30,356
is here under the Ministry of Health,

28
00:01:30,857 --> 00:01:32,192
Labour and Welfare.

29
00:01:32,859 --> 00:01:34,894
Yes, sir.

30
00:01:34,961 --> 00:01:38,298
Many organizations in different ministries

31
00:01:38,364 --> 00:01:43,903
export Japanese medical services.

32
00:01:43,970 --> 00:01:47,207
Authority is divided among the ministries.

33
00:01:47,273 --> 00:01:52,579
I must say the government's
growth strategy is just a fantasy.

34
00:01:53,179 --> 00:01:55,682
If they truly want the export of
medical services

35
00:01:55,748 --> 00:01:58,118
as a growth strategy,

36
00:01:58,918 --> 00:02:03,456
the authority held by the
ministries should be concentrated.

37
00:02:04,190 --> 00:02:06,960
Creating a new organization

38
00:02:07,026 --> 00:02:08,428
is an urgent matter.

39
00:02:09,696 --> 00:02:12,432
The Specified National R&D Corporation

40
00:02:12,999 --> 00:02:15,335
Japan Healthcare Organization.

41
00:02:16,402 --> 00:02:18,204
Here it is.

42
00:02:18,271 --> 00:02:20,273
JAPAN HEALTHCARE ORGANIZATION

43
00:02:20,340 --> 00:02:24,711
Mr. Tendo sure did
come up with a crazy idea.

44
00:02:25,078 --> 00:02:26,379
It's beyond a doctor's job.

45
00:02:29,382 --> 00:02:30,783
Is this a public viewing?

46
00:02:31,251 --> 00:02:32,218
What is it?

47
00:02:32,585 --> 00:02:34,487
I can't see, Demon.

48
00:02:34,921 --> 00:02:36,422
What did I do? Sorry.

49
00:02:38,291 --> 00:02:41,294
The unluckiest person today
is the Capricorn.

50
00:02:45,331 --> 00:02:47,033
Bad luck in work and everything.

51
00:02:47,100 --> 00:02:48,801
What are you doing?

52
00:02:50,503 --> 00:02:52,739
Such a scary face.

53
00:02:53,673 --> 00:02:54,541
Right?

54
00:02:54,607 --> 00:02:55,542
Mr. Tendo.

55
00:02:56,809 --> 00:03:01,381
In a structure where authority
is concentrated to one place,

56
00:03:01,915 --> 00:03:05,718
won't the patients in
the weak position be abandoned?

57
00:03:06,920 --> 00:03:09,756
Besides, is the Care Center

58
00:03:09,822 --> 00:03:11,658
that you are the president of

59
00:03:12,625 --> 00:03:15,595
even fulfilling its true mission?

60
00:03:16,229 --> 00:03:17,597
Excuse me?

61
00:03:17,664 --> 00:03:21,801
The power struggle between
Totei and Seikyo universities

62
00:03:21,868 --> 00:03:23,636
is unresolved.

63
00:03:24,137 --> 00:03:27,373
Why is he bringing this up?

64
00:03:28,875 --> 00:03:33,079
You integrated the two by name,
but nothing has changed.

65
00:03:36,749 --> 00:03:37,784
I found him.

66
00:03:38,484 --> 00:03:39,752
That's not it.

67
00:03:40,253 --> 00:03:46,659
There are rumors that you pay
a huge fee to a freelance surgeon.

68
00:03:46,726 --> 00:03:47,994
He's gone to the part-timer.

69
00:03:49,762 --> 00:03:51,097
Shut up, Daimon.

70
00:03:52,031 --> 00:03:53,466
How scary.

71
00:03:53,533 --> 00:03:58,071
It's a hospital that supposedly
has world-class doctors.

72
00:03:58,137 --> 00:04:00,006
How does it end up like this?

73
00:04:01,140 --> 00:04:02,308
There's more.

74
00:04:02,375 --> 00:04:03,643
Mr. Tendo,

75
00:04:04,277 --> 00:04:07,113
after becoming the president,

76
00:04:07,180 --> 00:04:10,750
you have already
fired two doctors in a month.

77
00:04:11,918 --> 00:04:14,854
What is the meaning of this?

78
00:04:14,921 --> 00:04:16,789
That's not important.

79
00:04:17,323 --> 00:04:19,025
This guy is bad news.

80
00:04:19,492 --> 00:04:21,394
The two doctors who quit

81
00:04:21,995 --> 00:04:27,100
decided themselves and
turned in a letter of resignation.

82
00:04:27,900 --> 00:04:31,004
I did not fire them.

83
00:04:31,504 --> 00:04:33,072
Very suspicious.

84
00:04:33,506 --> 00:04:38,678
You always speak
about innovation and reform,

85
00:04:39,245 --> 00:04:42,115
but in reality, no one can disobey you.

86
00:04:42,749 --> 00:04:43,816
Are you trying to

87
00:04:43,883 --> 00:04:46,319
create an organization of servants?

88
00:04:46,386 --> 00:04:49,289
Yes! Yes!

89
00:04:49,355 --> 00:04:50,189
Daimon!

90
00:04:50,256 --> 00:04:51,090
Shut up!

91
00:04:51,591 --> 00:04:54,961
<i>This is a story about</i>
<i>a maverick female doctor.</i>

92
00:04:55,528 --> 00:04:56,863
<i>In 2014,</i>

93
00:04:57,297 --> 00:05:00,133
<i>medical establishments collapsed</i>
<i>and became more corrupt.</i>

94
00:05:01,134 --> 00:05:03,236
<i>Medicine, which handles lives,</i>

95
00:05:03,770 --> 00:05:07,273
<i>had strayed away from what it should be.</i>

96
00:05:07,340 --> 00:05:09,475
If you disagree,

97
00:05:10,109 --> 00:05:14,380
why not show the people that
your Care Center is superior?

98
00:05:14,814 --> 00:05:16,482
How about doing that?

99
00:05:16,549 --> 00:05:18,851
<i>However, despite these conditions,</i>

100
00:05:19,285 --> 00:05:23,356
<i>Japan announced to export</i>
<i>state of the art medical services</i>

101
00:05:23,423 --> 00:05:26,192
<i>as a growth strategy.</i>

102
00:05:26,259 --> 00:05:30,363
<i>Healthcare entered an era</i>
<i>of strong preying on the weak.</i>

103
00:05:30,430 --> 00:05:34,634
I don't quite understand what you mean.

104
00:05:38,004 --> 00:05:39,238
Currently,

105
00:05:41,474 --> 00:05:43,509
I have anaplastic thyroid cancer.

106
00:05:46,612 --> 00:05:51,250
<i>Then came freelance doctors</i>
<i>who don't belong to hospitals.</i>

107
00:05:51,317 --> 00:05:54,954
<i>In other words, maverick doctors.</i>

108
00:05:55,021 --> 00:05:55,988
Go to commercials?

109
00:05:56,723 --> 00:05:58,057
No.

110
00:05:58,124 --> 00:06:00,860
This cancer advances quickly.

111
00:06:01,494 --> 00:06:04,997
The 1-year survival rate is under 20%.

112
00:06:05,064 --> 00:06:06,999
Most die within 6 months.

113
00:06:08,167 --> 00:06:09,535
While I am speaking,

114
00:06:09,602 --> 00:06:11,237
the tumor

115
00:06:11,304 --> 00:06:14,207
is growing inside of me.

116
00:06:15,475 --> 00:06:16,876
Every hospital

117
00:06:17,410 --> 00:06:20,913
told me that
a radical operation is impossible.

118
00:06:27,854 --> 00:06:31,824
Could I get surgery? At your hospital?

119
00:06:34,994 --> 00:06:36,763
Can you cure my cancer?

120
00:06:39,465 --> 00:06:43,202
Your Care Center
is a great hospital, right?

121
00:06:43,636 --> 00:06:47,807
Then instead of creating a new authority,

122
00:06:47,874 --> 00:06:50,476
how about proving to everyone that

123
00:06:50,543 --> 00:06:52,979
your hospital is superior?

124
00:06:53,513 --> 00:06:55,448
What is he talking about?

125
00:06:55,882 --> 00:06:56,983
Can you?

126
00:06:57,049 --> 00:06:59,218
<i>For example, this woman.</i>

127
00:06:59,886 --> 00:07:03,222
<i>She hates groups,</i>
<i>authority, and being controlled.</i>

128
00:07:03,556 --> 00:07:06,859
<i>Her medical license and experience</i>

129
00:07:06,926 --> 00:07:08,194
<i>are her only weapons.</i>

130
00:07:08,594 --> 00:07:09,562
Your hospital...

131
00:07:10,329 --> 00:07:11,531
I'll cut him.

132
00:07:14,066 --> 00:07:16,569
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon,</i>

133
00:07:16,636 --> 00:07:19,772
<i>also known as Doctor-X.</i>

134
00:07:48,501 --> 00:07:51,871
We will begin the preoperative conference.

135
00:07:52,572 --> 00:07:54,974
The first case is Hiroshi Yomo,

136
00:07:55,041 --> 00:07:56,609
57 years old.

137
00:07:57,310 --> 00:08:00,279
The diagnosis is anaplastic
thyroid cancer,

138
00:08:00,947 --> 00:08:02,148
Stage IV-B.

139
00:08:02,648 --> 00:08:05,485
1-year survival rate is under 20%...

140
00:08:05,551 --> 00:08:07,787
Radical operation is impossible...

141
00:08:09,589 --> 00:08:10,923
Well...

142
00:08:10,990 --> 00:08:12,358
As you all know,

143
00:08:12,425 --> 00:08:16,462
Mr. Yomo is a journalist
known by everyone in Japan.

144
00:08:16,529 --> 00:08:19,499
And he challenged us

145
00:08:19,565 --> 00:08:21,734
on national television.

146
00:08:22,401 --> 00:08:24,871
We must win this battle.

147
00:08:25,438 --> 00:08:28,007
Please focus and work hard.

148
00:08:29,141 --> 00:08:30,610
- Mr. Tendo.
- Mr. Tendo.

149
00:08:30,676 --> 00:08:33,746
The thyroid gland is the West's specialty,

150
00:08:33,813 --> 00:08:35,748
so they can operate.

151
00:08:35,815 --> 00:08:38,684
No, the East is much better.
We don't have a specialist.

152
00:08:38,751 --> 00:08:41,787
I'm sorry, but I asking the East to do it.

153
00:08:42,488 --> 00:08:43,523
Stop this.

154
00:08:43,956 --> 00:08:46,158
You fight over profitable operations,

155
00:08:46,225 --> 00:08:48,461
yet avoid difficult ones.

156
00:08:49,128 --> 00:08:51,898
Such meaningless battles

157
00:08:52,365 --> 00:08:54,233
are creating a misunderstanding.

158
00:08:57,203 --> 00:09:00,740
The surgeon has already been decided on.

159
00:09:02,975 --> 00:09:05,244
It's neither East nor West.

160
00:09:06,445 --> 00:09:10,149
I have asked a doctor
in a neutral position.

161
00:09:11,684 --> 00:09:12,952
Neutral?

162
00:09:15,087 --> 00:09:18,124
Ikawa, please call the doctor.

163
00:09:18,190 --> 00:09:19,025
Yes.

164
00:09:21,227 --> 00:09:23,629
Kaji, Daimon's not here.

165
00:09:25,531 --> 00:09:26,465
Is it the demon?

166
00:09:36,576 --> 00:09:37,443
Hello.

167
00:09:38,277 --> 00:09:39,378
Greetings.

168
00:09:41,447 --> 00:09:43,115
How's it going?

169
00:09:47,653 --> 00:09:48,654
Hara?

170
00:09:48,988 --> 00:09:50,089
You know him?

171
00:09:50,156 --> 00:09:51,857
An old colleague.

172
00:09:51,924 --> 00:09:53,659
He's just a timid guy.

173
00:09:54,160 --> 00:09:55,227
Colleague?

174
00:09:59,065 --> 00:10:00,433
Welcome

175
00:10:00,967 --> 00:10:03,402
Thank you for inviting me.

176
00:10:04,570 --> 00:10:05,738
Let me introduce you.

177
00:10:07,039 --> 00:10:12,812
This is Dr. Mamoru Hara,
here from Vladivostok's Japan-Russia

178
00:10:12,878 --> 00:10:14,847
Advanced Medical Care Center.

179
00:10:16,015 --> 00:10:17,483
Russia?

180
00:10:17,550 --> 00:10:21,020
Dr. Hara is a thyroid specialist.

181
00:10:21,087 --> 00:10:24,123
He carried out several operations

182
00:10:24,190 --> 00:10:26,626
at the Japan-Russia Care Center.

183
00:10:27,760 --> 00:10:30,096
I'm Hara.

184
00:10:30,162 --> 00:10:32,665
I have strived

185
00:10:33,265 --> 00:10:37,036
for warm healthcare
that cares for the patient's soul.

186
00:10:37,103 --> 00:10:39,805
That is what got me to where I am today.

187
00:10:42,141 --> 00:10:44,844
I would like for you all to do the same.

188
00:10:48,280 --> 00:10:50,182
He's acting big.

189
00:10:50,249 --> 00:10:51,484
Different guy?

190
00:10:51,917 --> 00:10:52,785
How stupid.

191
00:10:52,852 --> 00:10:55,187
I will explain the operative method.

192
00:10:55,955 --> 00:10:59,358
The tumor has invaded the trachea,

193
00:10:59,425 --> 00:11:01,260
with lymph node metastasis.

194
00:11:01,327 --> 00:11:05,131
To save the patient,
I suggest total thyroidectomy

195
00:11:05,197 --> 00:11:08,300
and cervical lymphadenectomy.

196
00:11:08,868 --> 00:11:10,569
This is the best choice.

197
00:11:11,303 --> 00:11:16,876
The assistants will be...
Dr. Ebina and Dr. Dangozaka.

198
00:11:18,544 --> 00:11:22,948
Please cooperate with
each other and support Dr. Hara.

199
00:11:23,716 --> 00:11:24,550
Yes, sir.

200
00:11:25,584 --> 00:11:26,485
Yes, sir.

201
00:11:26,552 --> 00:11:27,520
Yes, sir.

202
00:11:28,621 --> 00:11:29,622
Yes, sir.

203
00:11:30,189 --> 00:11:33,159
Why are you leaving me out?

204
00:11:33,225 --> 00:11:34,860
Daimon!

205
00:11:35,227 --> 00:11:37,129
You're no longer a match for me.

206
00:11:37,196 --> 00:11:39,365
Long time no see, Daimon.

207
00:11:40,766 --> 00:11:41,600
Who are you?

208
00:11:43,502 --> 00:11:45,905
Anyway, I'll take this patient.

209
00:11:47,306 --> 00:11:48,307
Dr. Daimon,

210
00:11:48,874 --> 00:11:51,444
I know that you are extremely skilled.

211
00:11:51,510 --> 00:11:54,914
However, I cannot
have you do this operation.

212
00:11:55,581 --> 00:11:56,415
Why?

213
00:11:56,482 --> 00:11:58,117
Didn't you see the show?

214
00:11:58,818 --> 00:12:00,586
We can't have more rumors

215
00:12:00,653 --> 00:12:02,455
about a part-timer.

216
00:12:02,521 --> 00:12:03,956
But it's true.

217
00:12:04,990 --> 00:12:06,659
Arrogant as always.

218
00:12:06,726 --> 00:12:07,760
Get out!

219
00:12:08,694 --> 00:12:09,528
Who are you?

220
00:12:10,596 --> 00:12:12,732
Get her out!

221
00:12:12,798 --> 00:12:13,699
Yes, sir.

222
00:12:17,470 --> 00:12:20,106
It hurts! Ouch!

223
00:12:20,172 --> 00:12:21,073
That's enough!

224
00:12:22,541 --> 00:12:24,376
I remember this now.

225
00:12:28,347 --> 00:12:30,149
I'm back!

226
00:12:32,485 --> 00:12:34,386
Sorry, it's nothing.

227
00:12:38,858 --> 00:12:39,692
I can't remember.

228
00:12:40,359 --> 00:12:41,694
Who is that?

229
00:12:43,129 --> 00:12:45,698
Where have I seen him?

230
00:12:45,765 --> 00:12:48,968
Michiko! Michiko!

231
00:12:49,034 --> 00:12:49,902
Akira!

232
00:12:49,969 --> 00:12:51,470
What...

233
00:12:51,537 --> 00:12:52,638
Over here.

234
00:12:52,705 --> 00:12:55,341
What's wrong?

235
00:12:55,407 --> 00:12:58,410
I can't see because of the tears.

236
00:13:00,846 --> 00:13:02,281
PRIVATE ROOM B

237
00:13:02,348 --> 00:13:03,783
ALBERTO SAVAROTTI

238
00:13:03,849 --> 00:13:06,051
He lost his voice.

239
00:13:06,118 --> 00:13:07,620
His show was cancelled.

240
00:13:08,387 --> 00:13:09,688
You saved us,

241
00:13:09,755 --> 00:13:12,024
but please don't tell the media.

242
00:13:12,091 --> 00:13:13,159
Of course.

243
00:13:13,225 --> 00:13:15,694
I asked the hospital

244
00:13:15,761 --> 00:13:17,429
to keep everything confidential.

245
00:13:17,496 --> 00:13:19,498
"Grazie." Thank you.

246
00:13:19,565 --> 00:13:22,234
Don't worry about the fees.

247
00:13:22,301 --> 00:13:23,269
We'll pay...

248
00:13:23,836 --> 00:13:24,703
What?

249
00:13:25,204 --> 00:13:30,009
Instead, when he's cured,
have him sing for me.

250
00:13:30,075 --> 00:13:30,943
Hey!

251
00:13:31,510 --> 00:13:33,612
What are you whispering about?

252
00:13:33,679 --> 00:13:35,080
Not your business.

253
00:13:35,681 --> 00:13:36,715
How suspicious.

254
00:13:36,782 --> 00:13:37,850
You handle that.

255
00:13:40,152 --> 00:13:42,655
Papillary thyroid cancer.

256
00:13:44,957 --> 00:13:46,826
I'd say Stage III.

257
00:13:47,693 --> 00:13:50,729
There's vocal cord paralysis.

258
00:13:50,796 --> 00:13:52,131
This is urgent.

259
00:13:52,765 --> 00:13:56,035
Savarotti's voice is the world's treasure.

260
00:13:56,101 --> 00:13:58,671
If surgery fails... Mamma mia!

261
00:13:59,038 --> 00:14:02,374
<i>Don't worry. This doctor doesn't fail.</i>

262
00:14:03,042 --> 00:14:07,213
Don't worry. This doctor doesn't fail.

263
00:14:15,187 --> 00:14:18,757
This operation is a tough case.

264
00:14:18,824 --> 00:14:20,759
I understand that.

265
00:14:21,827 --> 00:14:24,430
That's why I called you.

266
00:14:26,031 --> 00:14:26,866
Yes.

267
00:14:26,932 --> 00:14:29,401
The media is paying attention.

268
00:14:30,202 --> 00:14:31,203
Yes.

269
00:14:31,270 --> 00:14:34,106
You must save his life...

270
00:14:36,442 --> 00:14:38,244
Just his life.

271
00:14:44,550 --> 00:14:45,384
Yes, sir.

272
00:14:46,785 --> 00:14:47,853
Why?

273
00:14:47,920 --> 00:14:49,488
The hospital he worked at

274
00:14:49,989 --> 00:14:52,324
is a colony of Totei University.

275
00:14:52,391 --> 00:14:55,261
And he was just at the 3rd branch.

276
00:14:56,462 --> 00:14:59,198
Why was he chosen
for this important surgery?

277
00:15:00,599 --> 00:15:05,437
That journalist's statements
have a great impact on society.

278
00:15:06,505 --> 00:15:10,743
And now... That man is opposing

279
00:15:11,644 --> 00:15:13,812
Mr. Tendo's healthcare reform.

280
00:15:15,848 --> 00:15:19,418
And they're cutting into
this man's throat...

281
00:15:22,521 --> 00:15:23,355
No way.

282
00:15:25,257 --> 00:15:27,793
If that's true...

283
00:15:32,298 --> 00:15:34,433
An easily controllable man is needed.

284
00:15:36,001 --> 00:15:37,503
Hara is perfect.

285
00:15:42,308 --> 00:15:43,142
Excuse me.

286
00:15:46,178 --> 00:15:47,179
What is it?

287
00:15:48,347 --> 00:15:49,415
I'll make this clear.

288
00:15:50,582 --> 00:15:53,652
I won't take part
in futile power struggles.

289
00:15:55,421 --> 00:16:00,092
I'm sure the East and West
are already fighting over me.

290
00:16:00,159 --> 00:16:02,461
I thought it'd be best to refuse early.

291
00:16:04,630 --> 00:16:06,932
You came to say that?

292
00:16:06,999 --> 00:16:07,833
Yes.

293
00:16:09,001 --> 00:16:11,637
If you wish to gain progress like me,

294
00:16:12,071 --> 00:16:14,807
leave the country and train yourselves.

295
00:16:15,240 --> 00:16:17,009
Becoming an individual

296
00:16:17,643 --> 00:16:19,345
who can handle any surgery

297
00:16:19,778 --> 00:16:22,281
is your only way to worldwide acclaim.

298
00:16:22,881 --> 00:16:24,516
- I think...
- That's all.

299
00:16:24,583 --> 00:16:25,617
Thank you.

300
00:16:37,763 --> 00:16:38,630
Yes?

301
00:16:45,971 --> 00:16:51,410
In order to change yourself,
change your reflection in the mirror.

302
00:16:52,378 --> 00:16:53,312
What?

303
00:16:58,684 --> 00:17:00,552
He is absolutely unbearable.

304
00:17:01,820 --> 00:17:03,655
He emanates misery.

305
00:17:05,958 --> 00:17:09,928
Oh, I've been waiting for this.

306
00:17:16,068 --> 00:17:17,002
Excuse me.

307
00:17:23,609 --> 00:17:26,178
I should've gotten shrimp tempura.

308
00:17:26,879 --> 00:17:31,183
When you get what you desire,
you'll get a new desire.

309
00:17:31,250 --> 00:17:32,117
That's how it is.

310
00:17:33,018 --> 00:17:36,255
- What?
- Humans are greedy.

311
00:17:36,321 --> 00:17:40,025
Yet they fear the risks
of trying something new,

312
00:17:40,092 --> 00:17:42,861
and overly accept
their current dissatisfaction.

313
00:17:42,928 --> 00:17:44,129
That should be enough.

314
00:17:45,731 --> 00:17:48,434
But that's dangerous.

315
00:17:48,967 --> 00:17:50,436
Don't tolerate dissatisfaction.

316
00:17:50,936 --> 00:17:53,205
- We are constantly...
- Shut up.

317
00:17:56,575 --> 00:17:57,709
Do you know me?

318
00:18:05,651 --> 00:18:09,888
Thyroid cancer, Stage 4B.
You picked a fight with this place.

319
00:18:09,955 --> 00:18:12,458
Not a fight. A challenge.

320
00:18:14,726 --> 00:18:15,861
I'll cut you.

321
00:18:18,030 --> 00:18:19,932
I can completely cure you.

322
00:18:21,066 --> 00:18:23,235
This is a battle with the hospital.

323
00:18:23,302 --> 00:18:25,170
I can't ask you.

324
00:18:26,538 --> 00:18:27,639
How brave.

325
00:18:29,174 --> 00:18:30,042
What do you mean?

326
00:18:30,576 --> 00:18:33,745
The surgeon sucks compared to me.

327
00:18:35,314 --> 00:18:36,982
Hey,

328
00:18:37,049 --> 00:18:38,584
stop talking while you eat.

329
00:18:39,084 --> 00:18:40,452
Mr. Yomo,

330
00:18:40,953 --> 00:18:43,455
I have brought the informed consent.

331
00:18:44,123 --> 00:18:45,057
You suck?

332
00:18:45,591 --> 00:18:46,525
Excuse me?

333
00:18:47,626 --> 00:18:48,494
I'm good.

334
00:18:52,631 --> 00:18:53,465
What?

335
00:18:54,333 --> 00:18:55,534
Expensive.

336
00:18:56,502 --> 00:18:57,336
What is?

337
00:18:57,936 --> 00:18:59,338
Too expensive.

338
00:19:03,442 --> 00:19:05,310
SHRIMP TEMPURA 180 YEN

339
00:19:06,845 --> 00:19:07,813
The shrimp tempura?

340
00:19:09,481 --> 00:19:11,416
KANBARA DOCTOR AGENCY

341
00:19:12,751 --> 00:19:13,552
Pong!

342
00:19:14,052 --> 00:19:16,655
A normal doctor would be too scared

343
00:19:16,722 --> 00:19:19,258
to cut Savarotti's throat.

344
00:19:19,324 --> 00:19:20,325
Why?

345
00:19:20,392 --> 00:19:23,595
They say Savarotti has the voice of god.

346
00:19:23,662 --> 00:19:26,498
He has devoted followers everywhere.

347
00:19:26,832 --> 00:19:30,269
What if you accidentally
cut his vocal cord?

348
00:19:30,669 --> 00:19:32,604
Don't say "accidentally cut."

349
00:19:32,671 --> 00:19:35,674
If you cut his recurrent nerve...

350
00:19:35,741 --> 00:19:36,575
I'll kill you.

351
00:19:36,642 --> 00:19:37,876
I'm scared.

352
00:19:37,943 --> 00:19:39,678
Michiko's fine.

353
00:19:39,745 --> 00:19:43,182
The one who might
mess up is the other doctor.

354
00:19:43,248 --> 00:19:45,050
I think so too.

355
00:19:45,117 --> 00:19:47,486
Even if he got better,
it's still Dr. Hara,

356
00:19:47,553 --> 00:19:48,987
after all.

357
00:19:49,388 --> 00:19:51,490
Maybe it's fine if he does.

358
00:19:52,624 --> 00:19:53,592
What do you mean?

359
00:19:58,730 --> 00:20:01,200
- Not that one.
- Shut up.

360
00:20:01,266 --> 00:20:03,202
- You've done it.
- What?

361
00:20:03,268 --> 00:20:07,072
Ron. 32,000 points!

362
00:20:07,139 --> 00:20:08,740
You messed up.

363
00:20:08,807 --> 00:20:13,712
Will I ever win?

364
00:20:22,020 --> 00:20:22,854
Everyone.

365
00:20:24,156 --> 00:20:26,625
I will go to the surgery room now.

366
00:20:27,292 --> 00:20:31,797
I will risk my life
to show you Japan's best hospital.

367
00:20:31,863 --> 00:20:35,267
Death comes equally to all humans.

368
00:20:36,368 --> 00:20:38,370
Ever since the start of humanity,

369
00:20:38,437 --> 00:20:41,006
no one has escaped death.

370
00:20:42,908 --> 00:20:46,778
And I feel that
it should always be this way.

371
00:20:47,212 --> 00:20:48,247
That is why

372
00:20:49,248 --> 00:20:51,183
I do not fear death at all.

373
00:20:53,685 --> 00:20:55,554
I hope that I will see you again.

374
00:20:58,557 --> 00:21:02,361
I am being taken to
the surgery room on a stretcher.

375
00:21:02,427 --> 00:21:05,998
This world-class hospital

376
00:21:06,064 --> 00:21:08,567
seems to be equipped well.

377
00:21:08,634 --> 00:21:10,602
You cannot film past this point.

378
00:21:10,669 --> 00:21:11,970
Give me the camera.

379
00:21:12,037 --> 00:21:12,904
- Really?
- Yes.

380
00:21:13,272 --> 00:21:14,740
- Save the data.
- Yes.

381
00:21:15,407 --> 00:21:16,308
Thank you.

382
00:21:43,902 --> 00:21:46,405
Success brings joy to life.

383
00:21:47,272 --> 00:21:50,242
Let there be joy in everyone's life.

384
00:21:51,410 --> 00:21:53,045
What happened to this man?

385
00:21:55,547 --> 00:21:56,548
Let's begin.

386
00:21:57,215 --> 00:21:58,984
Total thyroidectomy

387
00:21:59,051 --> 00:22:00,585
and cervical lymphadenectomy.

388
00:22:00,652 --> 00:22:01,586
- Scalpel.
- Yes.

389
00:22:02,154 --> 00:22:03,055
- Forceps.
- Yes.

390
00:22:04,956 --> 00:22:05,857
It's begun.

391
00:22:14,466 --> 00:22:17,669
We will remove the thyroid's left lobe.

392
00:22:17,736 --> 00:22:21,039
Blood pressure 100. Pulse 60 and sinus.

393
00:22:27,913 --> 00:22:30,148
Who's playing the music? Who?

394
00:22:30,782 --> 00:22:32,284
I'm counting on you.

395
00:22:32,351 --> 00:22:34,152
It's too loud.

396
00:22:34,219 --> 00:22:35,253
OK!

397
00:22:37,255 --> 00:22:39,658
Pull the thyroid up.

398
00:22:40,025 --> 00:22:41,126
- Pean.
- Yes.

399
00:22:45,664 --> 00:22:48,633
The tumor has invaded the recurrent nerve.

400
00:22:48,700 --> 00:22:50,102
It's worse than expected.

401
00:22:50,736 --> 00:22:54,539
Removal while preserving
the nerve is impossible.

402
00:22:56,208 --> 00:22:57,109
What will you do?

403
00:22:58,310 --> 00:22:59,511
If you cut the nerve...

404
00:23:05,584 --> 00:23:06,918
His life is the top priority.

405
00:23:14,092 --> 00:23:15,827
We will remove the recurrent nerve.

406
00:23:17,095 --> 00:23:18,130
- Cooper.
- Yes.

407
00:23:39,317 --> 00:23:41,686
Sutures complete. Blood loss?

408
00:23:41,753 --> 00:23:42,654
Minimal.

409
00:23:43,021 --> 00:23:44,089
We're done.

410
00:23:44,156 --> 00:23:45,357
Thank you.

411
00:23:58,737 --> 00:23:59,771
Thank you.

412
00:24:00,639 --> 00:24:01,473
Good job.

413
00:24:05,544 --> 00:24:07,579
Michiko,

414
00:24:07,646 --> 00:24:09,247
that was perfect!

415
00:24:09,314 --> 00:24:11,550
Bravo!

416
00:24:15,120 --> 00:24:17,155
We will close the wound. Stapler.

417
00:24:32,404 --> 00:24:33,371
We're done.

418
00:24:33,438 --> 00:24:36,141
The cancer has been completely removed.

419
00:24:38,710 --> 00:24:39,845
Thank you.

420
00:24:40,479 --> 00:24:41,813
Thank you.

421
00:24:42,581 --> 00:24:43,682
Well done.

422
00:24:44,115 --> 00:24:44,983
Thank you

423
00:24:51,790 --> 00:24:52,657
Wonderful.

424
00:24:53,325 --> 00:24:55,460
The hospital's reputation
will go up again.

425
00:25:14,079 --> 00:25:16,481
"Thank you very much.

426
00:25:16,548 --> 00:25:18,917
I got my voice back."

427
00:25:19,351 --> 00:25:21,019
"I owe it to you all."

428
00:25:24,956 --> 00:25:26,625
Yes, yes.

429
00:25:31,997 --> 00:25:34,399
"I will sing for you all."

430
00:25:34,966 --> 00:25:36,234
As promised.

431
00:25:36,701 --> 00:25:39,137
This is like a dream.

432
00:26:12,704 --> 00:26:15,507
What did you say after surgery?

433
00:26:16,541 --> 00:26:19,477
Please sing for Akira.

434
00:26:19,544 --> 00:26:21,146
- Really?
- Michiko,

435
00:26:21,212 --> 00:26:22,948
you are such a good girl.

436
00:26:23,014 --> 00:26:24,616
No. I said he's fat.

437
00:26:25,016 --> 00:26:25,917
You're terrible.

438
00:26:42,067 --> 00:26:43,101
What?

439
00:26:43,168 --> 00:26:45,637
Mr. Yomo is recovering

440
00:26:45,704 --> 00:26:47,072
and should be discharged soon.

441
00:26:47,939 --> 00:26:50,075
Your surgery was what I hoped for.

442
00:26:50,141 --> 00:26:51,943
I'm glad I called you.

443
00:26:52,010 --> 00:26:53,612
Thank you.

444
00:26:53,678 --> 00:26:56,781
We'd like to arrange a dinner tonight.

445
00:26:56,848 --> 00:26:57,916
Are you free?

446
00:26:57,983 --> 00:27:00,518
I'd love to.

447
00:27:05,323 --> 00:27:06,992
Excuse me.

448
00:27:09,427 --> 00:27:10,362
What is it?

449
00:27:10,428 --> 00:27:13,465
He said he's dissatisfied.

450
00:27:13,531 --> 00:27:14,466
Dissatisfied?

451
00:27:23,608 --> 00:27:24,643
"Complaint."

452
00:27:25,744 --> 00:27:27,245
"I have died.

453
00:27:28,446 --> 00:27:30,415
My voice is my life.

454
00:27:31,082 --> 00:27:33,151
My voice was taken away.

455
00:27:33,818 --> 00:27:37,222
Therefore, I will sue this hospital."

456
00:27:38,123 --> 00:27:39,057
Okay?

457
00:27:39,124 --> 00:27:40,291
Mr. Yomo,

458
00:27:40,692 --> 00:27:42,594
I explained before the surgery.

459
00:27:42,661 --> 00:27:45,230
Your voice may be lost to save your life.

460
00:27:46,097 --> 00:27:48,533
You accepted too.

461
00:27:49,601 --> 00:27:50,769
Here's the consent.

462
00:27:50,835 --> 00:27:52,037
SURGERY CONSENT FORM

463
00:27:52,103 --> 00:27:53,772
HIROSHI YOMO

464
00:27:53,838 --> 00:27:54,806
What can you do?

465
00:27:55,607 --> 00:27:57,642
He wants shrimp tempura too.

466
00:27:58,109 --> 00:27:58,943
Shrimp?

467
00:27:59,010 --> 00:28:02,947
When you get what you desire,
you'll get a new desire.

468
00:28:03,415 --> 00:28:04,616
That's how humans are.

469
00:28:04,683 --> 00:28:10,755
You should've said from the start
that you want your voice and your life.

470
00:28:16,528 --> 00:28:19,698
"This hospital took my voice on purpose.

471
00:28:19,764 --> 00:28:22,967
My voice was a problem for Mr. Tendo,

472
00:28:23,034 --> 00:28:25,437
as I opposed his healthcare reform."

473
00:28:27,172 --> 00:28:28,006
Really?

474
00:28:28,573 --> 00:28:29,607
That's ridiculous!

475
00:28:29,674 --> 00:28:31,476
How dare you.

476
00:28:31,543 --> 00:28:32,444
Mr. Tendo!

477
00:28:33,778 --> 00:28:34,846
In other words,

478
00:28:35,780 --> 00:28:39,617
you want your voice back. Is that right?

479
00:28:40,652 --> 00:28:42,687
Of course, right?

480
00:28:42,754 --> 00:28:43,955
He's not asking you.

481
00:28:46,124 --> 00:28:50,962
All other hospitals gave up on your life,
but we saved it.

482
00:28:51,830 --> 00:28:54,332
Because that was your request.

483
00:28:55,400 --> 00:29:00,538
And now, you have a new request
to have your voice back.

484
00:29:02,373 --> 00:29:06,644
We at the Care Center, in order to meet

485
00:29:07,145 --> 00:29:13,384
the requests of our patients...
Give our best effort.

486
00:29:13,451 --> 00:29:15,253
I'll do it.

487
00:29:15,320 --> 00:29:16,154
No.

488
00:29:17,222 --> 00:29:20,024
I can't have you do this operation either.

489
00:29:20,091 --> 00:29:20,992
Why?

490
00:29:21,059 --> 00:29:22,060
I told you.

491
00:29:22,127 --> 00:29:25,864
It doesn't look good
to pay a huge fee to a part-timer.

492
00:29:26,331 --> 00:29:29,300
I will ask Dr. Hara for
this operation as well.

493
00:29:31,136 --> 00:29:31,970
Me?

494
00:29:32,604 --> 00:29:34,906
Failure is not an option here.

495
00:29:35,940 --> 00:29:38,276
Do you understand what this means?

496
00:29:42,447 --> 00:29:43,381
Yes.

497
00:29:43,448 --> 00:29:47,819
We don't need doctors...
who cannot display superior skills.

498
00:29:51,823 --> 00:29:52,657
Mr. Yomo,

499
00:29:53,892 --> 00:29:57,362
about the two doctors
leaving this hospital within a month...

500
00:29:58,863 --> 00:30:00,398
This is why.

501
00:30:02,100 --> 00:30:06,671
Yes,
but the vocal cord nerves were already...

502
00:30:06,738 --> 00:30:08,473
Reconstruct them.

503
00:30:08,973 --> 00:30:09,841
Reconstruct?

504
00:30:11,743 --> 00:30:12,577
You can't do that?

505
00:30:17,682 --> 00:30:19,184
Who do you think I am?

506
00:30:19,617 --> 00:30:20,919
- Who?
- Hey!

507
00:30:22,187 --> 00:30:23,221
Michiko Daimon,

508
00:30:24,022 --> 00:30:28,159
I'll show you the skills
that I have gained overseas.

509
00:30:28,226 --> 00:30:29,294
Be my assistant.

510
00:30:29,627 --> 00:30:31,162
- What?
- Don't complain.

511
00:30:33,231 --> 00:30:35,733
Is that alright, Mr. Tendo?

512
00:30:39,337 --> 00:30:40,171
That will be fine.

513
00:30:52,483 --> 00:30:55,653
We will reconstruct the recurrent nerves.

514
00:30:56,087 --> 00:30:56,988
I'm the surgeon.

515
00:31:01,092 --> 00:31:03,294
Success brings joy...

516
00:31:03,361 --> 00:31:04,395
Forget that.

517
00:31:04,462 --> 00:31:05,296
Scalpel.

518
00:31:05,363 --> 00:31:06,898
I said I'm the surgeon.

519
00:31:10,501 --> 00:31:11,636
- Success...
- Cut it out.

520
00:31:12,203 --> 00:31:13,872
- Scalpel.
- Scalpel.

521
00:31:16,875 --> 00:31:17,909
- Mosquito.
- Yes.

522
00:31:25,316 --> 00:31:28,620
Was it alright to let TV cameras in here?

523
00:31:29,487 --> 00:31:34,492
I have no problems with
having them report the truth.

524
00:31:46,638 --> 00:31:48,973
Great auricular nerve next.

525
00:31:49,374 --> 00:31:50,642
- Hold on.
- What?

526
00:31:51,242 --> 00:31:52,877
I'm the surgeon!

527
00:31:52,944 --> 00:31:55,813
You're thinking of an autotransplant?

528
00:31:57,749 --> 00:31:58,816
Are you serious?

529
00:31:59,417 --> 00:32:01,920
The vocal cord's motor functions

530
00:32:01,986 --> 00:32:03,821
won't recover that way.

531
00:32:05,723 --> 00:32:08,159
What other way is there?

532
00:32:08,893 --> 00:32:11,663
Nerve regeneration conduit.

533
00:32:13,331 --> 00:32:15,300
Regeneration conduit?

534
00:32:17,735 --> 00:32:18,569
Yes.

535
00:32:21,205 --> 00:32:22,040
Excuse me.

536
00:32:22,106 --> 00:32:23,174
Please stop filming.

537
00:32:23,241 --> 00:32:25,677
Will the film crew leave?

538
00:32:27,412 --> 00:32:31,916
Aren't you obligated to
show the truth to people?

539
00:32:32,884 --> 00:32:33,851
Yeah.

540
00:32:41,459 --> 00:32:43,328
Here's the conduit.

541
00:32:43,394 --> 00:32:44,262
Thanks.

542
00:32:48,232 --> 00:32:49,133
Move.

543
00:32:50,601 --> 00:32:51,536
Move.

544
00:32:55,039 --> 00:32:56,274
Not the part-timer.

545
00:32:57,742 --> 00:32:58,910
Stop filming!

546
00:32:59,877 --> 00:33:01,012
Don't film a failure.

547
00:33:09,754 --> 00:33:12,156
I don't fail.

548
00:33:14,025 --> 00:33:14,959
Bring down my loupe.

549
00:33:15,026 --> 00:33:15,927
Yes.

550
00:33:17,462 --> 00:33:18,730
- No.11 scalpel.
- Yes.

551
00:33:19,263 --> 00:33:21,499
Nerve regeneration conduit?

552
00:33:22,734 --> 00:33:24,769
It's an artificial nerve.

553
00:33:25,803 --> 00:33:31,776
It aids peripheral nerve regeneration.
It's a highly advanced medical equipment.

554
00:33:33,077 --> 00:33:35,680
Connecting the recurrent nerve
and conduit.

555
00:33:35,747 --> 00:33:36,581
Yes.

556
00:33:41,886 --> 00:33:44,489
SURGERY TIME

557
00:33:49,527 --> 00:33:50,661
It's connected.

558
00:33:50,728 --> 00:33:53,197
Next is arytenoid adduction.

559
00:33:54,365 --> 00:33:55,199
What?

560
00:33:55,767 --> 00:33:59,103
I'm decreasing
the space in the vocal cord.

561
00:33:59,771 --> 00:34:00,638
Got it.

562
00:34:00,705 --> 00:34:01,539
- Scalpel.
- Yes.

563
00:34:31,202 --> 00:34:32,270
Done.

564
00:34:32,336 --> 00:34:34,072
Wait a few days for the drain.

565
00:34:34,138 --> 00:34:34,972
Okay.

566
00:34:47,485 --> 00:34:48,586
Thank you.

567
00:34:48,653 --> 00:34:49,654
Good job.

568
00:34:49,720 --> 00:34:51,989
Thank you.

569
00:34:56,794 --> 00:34:57,895
Unbelievable.

570
00:35:00,631 --> 00:35:05,403
Thanks to Japan's
state-of-the-art medical technique,

571
00:35:05,837 --> 00:35:08,806
I regained my life and voice.

572
00:35:09,540 --> 00:35:14,045
The National Advanced
Medical Care Center is wonderful.

573
00:35:14,112 --> 00:35:15,346
HIROSHI YOMO PRESS CONFERENCE

574
00:35:15,813 --> 00:35:19,717
I will admit my defeat, Mr. Tendo.

575
00:35:21,619 --> 00:35:26,357
We simply provided
medical care that fit your requests.

576
00:35:26,824 --> 00:35:31,095
It's not that we did anything special.

577
00:35:32,897 --> 00:35:37,301
The foundation of journalism
lies in anti-authority.

578
00:35:38,236 --> 00:35:42,373
Especially if it's
against something enormous.

579
00:35:42,940 --> 00:35:43,875
Yes.

580
00:35:45,276 --> 00:35:48,412
If the country is heading
in the wrong direction,

581
00:35:49,280 --> 00:35:53,518
I hope you will continue
to speak out against it.

582
00:35:55,052 --> 00:35:56,020
Of course.

583
00:35:57,388 --> 00:36:00,224
I will speak with this voice you gave me.

584
00:36:09,934 --> 00:36:13,437
YOMO'S MIRACULOUS RECOVERY

585
00:36:13,504 --> 00:36:16,607
He got Japan's
best journalist on his side.

586
00:36:17,808 --> 00:36:21,512
Maybe this is what
Mr. Tendo wanted all along.

587
00:36:22,246 --> 00:36:25,650
And so he had Hara
take away his voice once.

588
00:36:26,350 --> 00:36:27,385
If that's true,

589
00:36:28,586 --> 00:36:29,554
he's a scary man.

590
00:36:30,888 --> 00:36:32,990
<i>Since the founding of the care center...</i>

591
00:36:33,057 --> 00:36:33,891
Either way,

592
00:36:35,293 --> 00:36:36,594
what should we do with him?

593
00:36:39,197 --> 00:36:40,064
True.

594
00:36:43,267 --> 00:36:48,873
It's a miracle that
you still have your job.

595
00:36:51,442 --> 00:36:52,276
In Russia...

596
00:36:55,546 --> 00:36:56,380
They called me...

597
00:36:59,417 --> 00:37:01,519
"The miracle maker."

598
00:37:03,421 --> 00:37:04,255
How nice.

599
00:37:06,490 --> 00:37:08,993
Yes.

600
00:37:10,795 --> 00:37:14,732
Let's make this clear, Hara.

601
00:37:18,302 --> 00:37:19,403
Yes?

602
00:37:19,804 --> 00:37:24,575
Are you going to side
with the East or the West?

603
00:37:33,718 --> 00:37:35,419
You're from Totei University,

604
00:37:36,087 --> 00:37:37,688
so I'd say East.

605
00:37:38,189 --> 00:37:40,858
However, we believe in teamwork.

606
00:37:41,292 --> 00:37:43,794
We don't your "individual" skills.

607
00:37:43,861 --> 00:37:47,832
We don't need this
useless guy from Russia either.

608
00:37:50,434 --> 00:37:52,036
What are you doing to do, Hara?

609
00:37:53,738 --> 00:37:55,206
Quit the hospital?

610
00:38:04,815 --> 00:38:05,816
Well...

611
00:38:10,388 --> 00:38:13,924
What you all said...

612
00:38:18,629 --> 00:38:21,165
I will take it seriously.

613
00:38:23,067 --> 00:38:24,035
What's wrong?

614
00:38:25,469 --> 00:38:27,938
You people wouldn't understand.

615
00:38:30,174 --> 00:38:31,642
Do you, Mr. Kaji?

616
00:38:33,544 --> 00:38:34,679
I wanted to...

617
00:38:37,948 --> 00:38:42,219
Reform healthcare... With those hopes...

618
00:38:44,388 --> 00:38:48,526
I worked so hard...

619
00:38:52,963 --> 00:38:54,098
He's gone nuts.

620
00:38:58,035 --> 00:39:00,905
I will work with Daimon.

621
00:39:00,971 --> 00:39:02,006
I won't do that.

622
00:39:06,077 --> 00:39:07,244
I remember.

623
00:39:08,446 --> 00:39:09,447
You're Kin.

624
00:39:09,880 --> 00:39:12,650
We went to elementary school together.

625
00:39:12,717 --> 00:39:15,319
I'm not Kin!

626
00:39:30,634 --> 00:39:32,870
Here's the footage I promised.

627
00:39:38,275 --> 00:39:39,810
- Any copies?
- No.

628
00:39:41,112 --> 00:39:44,815
It's the only footage in
the world of that surgery room.

629
00:39:45,683 --> 00:39:47,952
Thank you.

630
00:39:59,130 --> 00:39:59,997
Mr. Tendo.

631
00:40:01,432 --> 00:40:02,500
There are those

632
00:40:03,401 --> 00:40:06,137
who take on for a huge fee,

633
00:40:06,570 --> 00:40:10,107
dangerous operations that have
low survival and success rates,

634
00:40:10,875 --> 00:40:14,145
and have no definitive operative methods.

635
00:40:16,247 --> 00:40:20,351
With a sense of respect
and cynicism, they're called...

636
00:40:22,052 --> 00:40:27,158
"Evil doctors who use people's lives..."
"Doctor X."

637
00:40:29,693 --> 00:40:32,029
Is she a Doctor X?

638
00:40:34,565 --> 00:40:36,500
I don't know.

639
00:40:40,037 --> 00:40:41,872
But I know one thing.

640
00:40:45,109 --> 00:40:47,545
These Doctor Xs...

641
00:40:48,179 --> 00:40:51,148
They've presented
operative methods and cures

642
00:40:51,816 --> 00:40:54,885
that have shocked the world of medicine.

643
00:40:59,457 --> 00:41:01,525
They are necessary evils.

644
00:41:04,528 --> 00:41:06,163
That's what Doctor Xs are.

645
00:41:09,967 --> 00:41:13,504
She hates groups,
authority, and being controlled.

646
00:41:13,571 --> 00:41:18,209
Her medical license
and experience are her only weapons.

647
00:41:21,078 --> 00:41:21,946
Excuse me.

648
00:41:23,714 --> 00:41:24,582
Knock...

649
00:41:24,648 --> 00:41:26,150
I have a question.

650
00:41:26,717 --> 00:41:27,551
Yes?

651
00:41:27,618 --> 00:41:29,820
- About that surgery.
- Yes?

652
00:41:29,887 --> 00:41:33,257
There were TV cameras in the surgery room.

653
00:41:34,592 --> 00:41:35,626
And?

654
00:41:35,693 --> 00:41:38,462
I became the surgeon.

655
00:41:39,096 --> 00:41:39,964
Blackmail?

656
00:41:40,764 --> 00:41:41,599
What?

657
00:41:41,665 --> 00:41:44,235
We will not give in to your requests.

658
00:41:46,670 --> 00:41:49,340
I want to know when the broadcast is.

659
00:41:49,840 --> 00:41:50,674
Broadcast?

660
00:41:51,876 --> 00:41:53,711
I've never been on TV.

661
00:41:56,013 --> 00:41:57,081
I can't wait.

662
00:41:58,415 --> 00:42:00,117
That footage will not be broadcast.

663
00:42:00,784 --> 00:42:01,619
What?

664
00:42:01,685 --> 00:42:03,621
There was a malfunction.

665
00:42:03,687 --> 00:42:04,522
Seriously?

666
00:42:05,055 --> 00:42:06,090
I'm sorry.

667
00:42:07,725 --> 00:42:09,960
I'm so shocked.

668
00:42:10,761 --> 00:42:11,662
Michiko.

669
00:42:12,930 --> 00:42:14,798
Akira!

670
00:42:17,668 --> 00:42:20,871
I won't be on TV.

671
00:42:20,938 --> 00:42:24,408
Michiko. I'll buy you
shrimp tempura later.

672
00:42:25,109 --> 00:42:26,010
Shrimp?

673
00:42:26,076 --> 00:42:27,278
Wait outside.

674
00:42:32,016 --> 00:42:33,150
Sorry about that.

675
00:42:36,053 --> 00:42:37,121
This is a melon.

676
00:42:41,525 --> 00:42:42,726
This is a bill.

677
00:42:47,464 --> 00:42:48,332
Let me see...

678
00:42:48,766 --> 00:42:50,568
Ten million!

679
00:42:50,634 --> 00:42:52,770
What is this ridiculous price?

680
00:42:53,270 --> 00:42:55,172
Didn't the coverage of the surgery

681
00:42:55,673 --> 00:42:59,743
have a great impact on this hospital?

682
00:43:00,945 --> 00:43:03,347
The price is far more reasonable

683
00:43:03,847 --> 00:43:07,818
than airing a commercial
on national television.

684
00:43:07,885 --> 00:43:09,486
Very well.

685
00:43:10,454 --> 00:43:12,456
We will deposit the money later.

686
00:43:12,523 --> 00:43:14,024
Thank you.

687
00:43:14,925 --> 00:43:18,729
Also. We have something to give you too.

688
00:43:19,730 --> 00:43:20,564
What is it?

689
00:43:21,398 --> 00:43:22,266
Ikawa.

690
00:43:22,333 --> 00:43:23,167
Yes.

691
00:43:25,436 --> 00:43:26,403
Here it is.

692
00:43:26,470 --> 00:43:30,841
You requested for Savarotti's care.
Here's the bill.

693
00:43:33,544 --> 00:43:35,679
What is this ridiculous price?

694
00:43:35,746 --> 00:43:40,050
We secretly hospitalized
a world-famous celebrity.

695
00:43:40,784 --> 00:43:45,789
You had a dream-like experience
as one of his fans too.

696
00:43:47,024 --> 00:43:52,963
I believe that it is
an absolutely reasonable price.

697
00:43:54,698 --> 00:43:56,900
Akira, are you done?

698
00:43:59,970 --> 00:44:01,271
Give me a melon.

699
00:44:02,373 --> 00:44:04,041
You can take that if you like.

700
00:44:07,011 --> 00:44:09,713
What's wrong?

701
00:44:14,451 --> 00:44:16,954
That president is stubborn.

702
00:44:18,589 --> 00:44:22,393
Don't feel so down just because
he rejected the melon.

703
00:44:23,127 --> 00:44:26,964
You wouldn't understand how I feel.

704
00:44:31,635 --> 00:44:33,504
Is something wrong?

705
00:44:33,937 --> 00:44:37,708
The only thing wrong is your huge debt.

706
00:44:38,208 --> 00:44:40,310
You're going to keep working hard.

707
00:44:41,378 --> 00:44:42,413
What?

708
00:44:43,113 --> 00:44:44,481
Hey, Akira.

709
00:44:46,216 --> 00:44:47,584
SHRIMP TEMPURA

710
00:44:47,651 --> 00:44:49,987
Akira, I want to eat shrimp tempura.

711
00:44:50,054 --> 00:44:52,589
Cancel that. No treats.

712
00:44:55,893 --> 00:44:59,029
He's coming back!

713
00:45:00,898 --> 00:45:02,199
SAVAROTTI'S RE-VISIT TO JAPAN

714
00:45:04,968 --> 00:45:09,506
Michiko, Savarotti is coming again.
Savarotti!

715
00:45:09,573 --> 00:45:12,409
- Savarotti!
- Forget Savarotti.

716
00:45:12,476 --> 00:45:15,312
I want shrimp tempura.

717
00:45:16,180 --> 00:45:18,382
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon,</i>

718
00:45:18,849 --> 00:45:21,919
<i>also known as Doctor-X.</i>

719
00:46:38,996 --> 00:46:42,666
One of you will step down as director.

720
00:46:42,733 --> 00:46:44,902
Whoever wins is strong.

721
00:46:44,968 --> 00:46:47,204
Forget doctors' battles.

722
00:46:47,271 --> 00:46:49,006
The patient has to win.

723
00:46:49,072 --> 00:46:51,775
Don't think it's over.
